{"resource": {"name": "Bacteria Sample Data", "id": "e49x-tw9b", "resource_name": null, "parent_fxf": [], "description": "Samples are taken daily at locations throughout the distribution system. Temperature, pH, and Total Chlorine Residual are collected by city personnel. Samples are taken to a lab to be analyzed for Total Coliform and E. Coli indicators. Results are returned to the city the following business day.", "attribution": null, "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2024-12-31T11:35:51.000Z", "createdAt": "2018-10-31T19:18:11.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2024-12-31T11:35:49.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2024-12-31T11:35:51.000Z", "columns_name": ["RESULTS", "DATE", "Replacement Address/Notes", "Sample Type", "Number of Samples Taken", "Total Chlorine Residual", "Street", "Free Chlorine", "SITE #"], "columns_field_name": ["results", "date", "replacement_address_or_notes", "replacement_sample", "number_of_samples_taken", "total_chlorine_residual", "street", "free_chlorine", "site"], "columns_datatype": ["Text", "Calendar date", "Text", "Text", "Number", "Number", "Text", "Number", "Text"], "columns_description": ["Provides results from the laboratory to indicate pass, fail, or if sample was rejected.", "Date test was conducted.", "Indicates the location of replacement samples, special samples, or any notes associated with the sample.", "Bacteria Samples are routine and collected every 30 days. If a sample has an error, is rejected, or has bacteria present, a replacement sample is taken. This column indicates if the sample is a replacement. Special Samples are locations that are not normally sampled. Refer to the notes section to determine why sample was taken.", "Number of samples taken at the location.", "The level of chlorine disinfectant by measuring chloramines (minimum requirement is .5 mg/L). Instruments have an accuracy of plus or minus 0.1 mg/L.", "Street name for where water sample was collected.", "The amou